nReason text for each:\n\np01 reason:\n\"Forward primer unique match at TX_CANONICAL:1; reverse primer unique match at TX_CANONICAL:83-102 (reverse complement); observed amplicon 102 bp vs expected 108 bp (length mismatch); amplicon spans seq positions 1-102, outside annotated CDS 101-700; METADATA INCONSISTENCY: TX_CANONICAL CDS=101-700 exceeds sequence length 102; forward primer also binds TX_ALT at position 1 without forming an amplicon.\"\n\np02 reason:\n\"Forward primer unique match at TX_ALT:4; reverse primer unique match at TX_ALT:83-102; observed amplicon 99 bp vs expected 104 bp (length mismatch); amplicon spans positions 4-102, outside annotated CDS 101-640; METADATA INCONSISTENCY: TX_ALT CDS=101-640 exceeds sequence length 102; forward primer also binds TX_CANONICAL at position 4 without forming an amplicon.\"\n\np03 reason:\n\"No match: forward primer (poly-A) and reverse primer (poly-T) have no exact binding sites on any supplied transcript; no amplicon possible.\"\n\nAlso, all pairs: expected transcript is present in FASTA — yes for all.\n\nAdditionally, for p01 and p03, expected product length > transcript length is impossible — worth mentioning: for p01, expected 108 > sequence length 102 (impossible for this transcript); p03: expected 120 > 102 (impossible). p02: expected 104 > max possible given primer binding positions (99). Can add \"expected product length exceeds transcript length\".\n\nHmm wait, for p02 the max amplicon length from position 4 is 99; but expected 104 < 102 = sequence length, so it's not impossible from length alone, just inconsistent with the binding positions. For p01: expected 108 > 102 → impossible regardless of primer position. Nice nuance for the report.\n\nNow let me write analysis.py. Clean, well-commented, standard library only. Then run it, verify the outputs, and finalize report.md.\n\nOne more consideration about CSV format: the spec specifies the header exactly as `pair_id,transcripts_matched,amplicon_length,cds_compatible,status,reason`. Use the csv module with default quoting (minimal) — the reason field contains commas/semicolons so it'll be quoted. Fine. Newlines in reason — avoid; use \"; \" separator.\n\nReport.md content:\n- Title, date, inputs\n- Methods summary (exact matching, orientation rules, amplicon definition, CDS policy — report only, no repair)\n- Input validation / metadata findings section (prominently!)\n- Per-pair results table + details\n- Summary of verdicts\n- Recommendations\n\nLet me write the script now. Have it emit both CSV and report.md deterministically.\n\nCode sketch:\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport csv, re, sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nINPUTS = ROOT / \"inputs\"\nOUTPUT = ROOT / \"output\"\n\nCOMP = {\"A\":\"T\",\"T\":\"A\",\"G\":\"C\",\"C\":\"G\"}\n\ndef revcomp(s): return \"\".join(COMP[b] for b in reversed(s))\n\ndef find_all(haystack, needle):\n    pos, out = 0, []\n    while True:\n        i = haystack.find(needle, pos)\n        if i < 0: return out\n        out.append(i + 1)  # 1-based\n        pos = i + 1\n\ndef parse_fasta(path):\n    records = {}   # id -> record\n    order = []\n    issues = []    # global / per-record issues\n    cur = None\n    with open(path) as fh:\n        for lineno, raw in enumerate(fh, 1):\n            line = raw.rstrip(\"\\n\")\n            if not line.strip():\n                continue\n            if line.startswith(\">\"):\n                header = line[1:].strip()\n                tokens = header.split()\n                tid = tokens[0] if tokens else f\"<empty-id line {lineno}>\"\n                desc = \" \".join(tokens[1:]) if len(tokens) > 1 else \"\"\n                cur = {\"id\": tid, \"header\": header, \"desc\": desc, \"seq\": \"\",\n                       \"line\": lineno, \"issues\": [], \"cds\": None}\n                if tid in records:\n                    cur[\"issues\"].append(f\"duplicate transcript id '{tid}'\")\n                    issues.append(f\"line {lineno}: duplicate transcript id '{tid}'\")\n                records[tid] = cur\n                order.append(tid)\n            else:\n                if cur is None:\n                    issues.append(f\"line {lineno}: sequence data before any FASTA header\")\n                    continue\n                seq = line.strip().upper()\n                bad = sorted(set(seq) - set(\"ACGT\"))\n                if bad:\n                    cur[\"issues\"].append(f\"line {lineno}: non-ACGT characters in sequence: {','.join(bad)}\")\n                cur[\"seq\"] += seq\n    for tid in order:\n        rec = records[tid]\n        if not rec[\"seq\"]:\n            rec[\"issues\"].append(\"empty sequence\")\n        # parse CDS metadata\n        m = re.search(r\"CDS=(\\d+)-(\\d+)\", rec[\"header\"])\n        if m:\n            s, e = int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2))\n            rec[\"cds\"] = (s, e)\n            n = len(rec[\"seq\"])\n            if not (1 <= s <= e):\n                rec[\"issues\"].append(f\"CDS coordinates invalid (start {s} > end {e})\")\n            if e > n:\n                rec[\"issues\"].append(f\"METADATA INCONSISTENCY: CDS end {e} exceeds sequence length {n}\")\n            elif s <= n and (e - s + 1) % 3 != 0:\n                rec[\"issues\"].append(f\"CDS length {e-s+1} not a multiple of 3\")\n            # start/stop codon checks only when coordinates fully inside sequence\n            if 1 <= s and e <= n and n > 0:\n                cds_seq = rec[\"seq\"][s-1:e]\n                if not cds_seq.startswith(\"ATG\"):\n                    rec[\"issues\"].append(\"annotated CDS does not begin with ATG\")\n                if cds_seq[-3:] not in (\"TAA\",\"TAG\",\"TGA\"):\n                    rec[\"issues\"].append(\"annotated CDS does not end with a stop codon\")\n        else:\n            rec[\"issues\"].append(\"no CDS annotation found in header\")\n    return records, order, issues\n```\n\nHmm wait, for our data: CD